  "title": "A box blur and a Sobel edge map by hand",
  "estimatedMinutes": 25,
  "instructions": "## Convolution on a tiny image\n\nAn image is a list of rows of grey values (0 to 255). Implement two filters on the **interior** pixels; border pixels (first and last row and column) are copied from the input for the blur and set to 0 for the edge map.\n\n1. `box_blur(img)`: each interior pixel becomes the mean of its 3×3 neighbourhood, **rounded to the nearest integer** (Python `round`).\n2. `sobel(img)`: for each interior pixel compute `gx = (r-1,c+1) + 2(r,c+1) + (r+1,c+1) - (r-1,c-1) - 2(r,c-1) - (r+1,c-1)` and `gy` the same with rows and columns swapped (bottom minus top); the output is `abs(gx) + abs(gy)`.\n\nReturn new lists; do not modify the input.",
  "config": {
    "language": "python"
  },
  "initialState": {
    "language": "python",
    "source": "def box_blur(img):\n    h, w = len(img), len(img[0])\n    out = [row[:] for row in img]\n    # for r in 1..h-2, c in 1..w-2: mean of the 3x3 block, rounded\n    return out\n\n\ndef sobel(img):\n    h, w = len(img), len(img[0])\n    out = [[0] * w for _ in range(h)]\n    # gx, gy on interior pixels; out = abs(gx) + abs(gy)\n    return out\n\n\nimg = [[0, 0, 0, 0], [0, 90, 90, 0], [0, 90, 90, 0], [0, 0, 0, 0]]\nfor row in box_blur(img):\n    print(row)\n"
  },
  "hints": [
    "Sum img[r+dr][c+dc] for dr, dc in -1..1 and divide by 9; round() gives the nearest integer (Python rounds .5 to even).",
    "gx weights column c+1 by (1, 2, 1) and column c-1 by (-1, -2, -1); gy weights row r+1 by (1, 2, 1) and row r-1 by (-1, -2, -1).",
    "Build the output separately so later pixels do not see already-blurred neighbours."
